# Autocall pricing with several vol models (Heston, Rough Volatility classical, Bergomi Rough Volatility...) and stochastic rates. 
Calibrated on SX5E and Euribor 3M (funding impact).

End-to-end framework for:
- Vanilla calibration on SX5E implied vol surface (Bloomberg export)
- Pricing structured products (Athena / Phoenix)
- Model comparison and model-consistent Greeks (Delta/Gamma + model-aware Vega/Vanna/Volga + curve DV01)

## Models implemented
- GBM (Black–Scholes)
- Heston
- rBergomi
- RFSV
- rough_fbm
- Heston + Hull–White (hybrid)

## Installation
From the repo root:
```bash
pip install -e 
```

## Calibration
Example (rBergomi):
```bash
pricer-calibrate --model rbergomi \
  --curve data/raw/EURvs3MEuribor-Funding.xlsx \
  --surface data/raw/OptionsSX5E.xlsx
```
## Pricing
Example (rBergomi):
```bash
pricer --model rbergomi --s0 100 \
  --curve data/raw/EURvs3MEuribor-Funding.xlsx \
  --surface data/raw/OptionsSX5E.xlsx
```
The script loads calib_<model>.json builds the model with the funding curve, prices the default structured product and prints price + SE + Greeks: Delta, Gamma and model-aware Vega/Vanna/Volga (e.g. v0 for Heston, xi0_level for rBergomi, rough_nu for rough models), curve DV01 via parallel shift of the discount curve (disc_rates_parallel).

## Tests
pytest -q

## Notes
Discounting uses the curve (DV01 computed by bumping the whole curve by 1bp).
Greeks use bump-and-reprice with Common Random Numbers for variance reduction.